# Keep the Docker build context small and secret-free.
#
# The build context is the PROJECT ROOT (see docker-compose.yml — the image needs
# both backend/ and frontend/), so without this file `docker build` ships ~370MB,
# almost all of it a Windows virtualenv that is useless inside a Linux image.
#
# The Dockerfile copies four explicit paths rather than `COPY . .`, so nothing
# secret reaches an image layer today. This file is the second line of defence:
# if that ever changes, .env still cannot get in.

# --- Secrets: must never enter an image layer ---
.env
.env.local
*.env
!.env.example

# --- Virtualenvs: platform-specific and huge (345MB) ---
backend/venv/
backend/.venv/
venv/
.venv/

# --- Local persistence: rebuilt at runtime, and App Runner storage is ephemeral ---
backend/data/
data/
*.sqlite3
*.db
semantic_cache.json

# --- Python build noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- VCS and editors ---
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Docs: not needed at runtime, and they invalidate the layer cache on edit ---
*.md
!README.md
